    "id": "SM-c2870156bd139ba4",
    "section": "reading",
    "skill": "Main idea",
    "q": "Which statement best captures the purpose of the passage?",
    "o": [
      "To evaluate the trial addressing missing information on storage dates and identify a more informative comparison.",
      "To provide detailed instructions for implementing the change at a seed exchange.",
      "To establish that a volunteer training session that occurred at the same time fully explains the reported observation.",
      "To compare the financial costs of several institutions facing missing information on storage dates."
    ],
    "e": "Gagasan utama mencakup masalah, hasil percobaan, dan pengujian lanjutan. Petunjuk teknis, kepastian penyebab alternatif, dan perbandingan biaya bukan fokus bacaan.",
    "origin": "original",
    "passage": {
      "id": "SM-DR-R-03",
      "title": "Seed records",
      "text": "A team at a seed exchange had been concerned about missing information on storage dates. The team added date fields to return cards. During a 7-week trial, more returned packets had dated records. Staff kept daily logs describing both the operation of the change and the conditions under which it was used. These records were intended to make the experience available for later examination, rather than leave the discussion dependent on the recollection of one unusually successful day.\n\nThe observation did not settle every question about the change. The result could also have been affected by a volunteer training session that occurred at the same time. A comparison between the period before the change and the period after it would therefore combine two differences: the new procedure and the surrounding conditions. Counting more observations of the same combination would make that combination better described, but would not by itself separate the contributions of its components. The team kept the outcome in the report while distinguishing the observation from a claim about its cause. In the revised report, the conditions were printed adjacent to the outcome table, so readers saw them together.\n\nThe proposed next investigation was to separate the effects of card design and training. The staff would define the outcome in the same way across the comparison and retain records of relevant conditions. A useful question was whether the observed difference would remain when those conditions were made comparable. This question was narrower than deciding whether the procedure was best for every institution, every user, or every future period. The proposed comparison would supply evidence about the specified setting; applying it elsewhere would require considering how that other setting differed."
    },
    "solution": {
      "steps": [
        "Gagasan utama mencakup masalah, hasil percobaan, dan pengujian lanjutan. Petunjuk teknis, kepastian penyebab alternatif, dan perbandingan biaya bukan fokus bacaan."
      ],
      "evidence": "The proposed next investigation was to separate the effects of card design and training."
    },
