    "id": "SM-3e5e3799194cca32",
    "section": "reading",
    "skill": "Main idea",
    "q": "Which statement best captures the purpose of the passage?",
    "o": [
      "To evaluate the trial addressing water being applied before unexpected rain and identify a more informative comparison.",
      "To provide detailed instructions for implementing the change at a rooftop garden.",
      "To establish that cooler weather that also reduced evaporation fully explains the reported observation.",
      "To compare the financial costs of several institutions facing water being applied before unexpected rain."
    ],
    "e": "Gagasan utama mencakup masalah, hasil percobaan, dan pengujian lanjutan. Petunjuk teknis, kepastian penyebab alternatif, dan perbandingan biaya bukan fokus bacaan.",
    "origin": "original",
    "passage": {
      "id": "SM-DR-R-06",
      "title": "Garden watering",
      "text": "A team at a rooftop garden had been concerned about water being applied before unexpected rain. The team checked a rain forecast before watering. During a 5-week trial, recorded water use fell. Staff kept daily logs describing both the operation of the change and the conditions under which it was used. These records were intended to make the experience available for later examination, rather than leave the discussion dependent on the recollection of one unusually successful day.\n\nThe observation did not settle every question about the change. The result could also have been affected by cooler weather that also reduced evaporation. A comparison between the period before the change and the period after it would therefore combine two differences: the new procedure and the surrounding conditions. Counting more observations of the same combination would make that combination better described, but would not by itself separate the contributions of its components. The team kept the outcome in the report while distinguishing the observation from a claim about its cause. The staff proposed observations on consecutive days, starting on Monday and continuing without interruption until Friday.\n\nThe proposed next investigation was to compare water use under similar weather conditions. The staff would define the outcome in the same way across the comparison and retain records of relevant conditions. A useful question was whether the observed difference would remain when those conditions were made comparable. This question was narrower than deciding whether the procedure was best for every institution, every user, or every future period. The proposed comparison would supply evidence about the specified setting; applying it elsewhere would require considering how that other setting differed."
    },
    "solution": {
      "steps": [
        "Gagasan utama mencakup masalah, hasil percobaan, dan pengujian lanjutan. Petunjuk teknis, kepastian penyebab alternatif, dan perbandingan biaya bukan fokus bacaan."
      ],
      "evidence": "The proposed next investigation was to compare water use under similar weather conditions."
    },
    "difficulty": "foundation",
    "drillOnly": true,
    "edition": "drills-2026-10",
    "drillIndex": 6
