    "id": "SM-fdf8a5a477289156",
    "section": "reading",
    "skill": "Main idea",
    "q": "Which statement best captures the purpose of the passage?",
    "o": [
      "To evaluate the trial addressing poor visibility at path junctions and identify a more informative comparison.",
      "To provide detailed instructions for implementing the change at a campus facilities team.",
      "To establish that more experienced users walking during the survey fully explains the reported observation.",
      "To compare the financial costs of several institutions facing poor visibility at path junctions."
    ],
    "e": "Gagasan utama mencakup masalah, hasil percobaan, dan pengujian lanjutan. Petunjuk teknis, kepastian penyebab alternatif, dan perbandingan biaya bukan fokus bacaan.",
    "origin": "original",
    "passage": {
      "id": "SM-DR-R-10",
      "title": "Path lighting",
      "text": "A team at a campus facilities team had been concerned about poor visibility at path junctions. The team redirected existing lights toward the junctions. During a 4-week trial, walkers reported fewer missed turns. Staff kept daily logs describing both the operation of the change and the conditions under which it was used. These records were intended to make the experience available for later examination, rather than leave the discussion dependent on the recollection of one unusually successful day.\n\nThe observation did not settle every question about the change. The result could also have been affected by more experienced users walking during the survey. A comparison between the period before the change and the period after it would therefore combine two differences: the new procedure and the surrounding conditions. Counting more observations of the same combination would make that combination better described, but would not by itself separate the contributions of its components. The team kept the outcome in the report while distinguishing the observation from a claim about its cause. Limited staff time was a constraint, so the proposed follow-up could not include every possible comparison.\n\nThe proposed next investigation was to compare new visitors using the old and new lighting. The staff would define the outcome in the same way across the comparison and retain records of relevant conditions. A useful question was whether the observed difference would remain when those conditions were made comparable. This question was narrower than deciding whether the procedure was best for every institution, every user, or every future period. The proposed comparison would supply evidence about the specified setting; applying it elsewhere would require considering how that other setting differed."
    },
    "solution": {
      "steps": [
        "Gagasan utama mencakup masalah, hasil percobaan, dan pengujian lanjutan. Petunjuk teknis, kepastian penyebab alternatif, dan perbandingan biaya bukan fokus bacaan."
      ],
      "evidence": "The proposed next investigation was to compare new visitors using the old and new lighting."
    },
    "difficulty": "foundation",
    "drillOnly": true,
    "edition": "drills-2026-10",
    "drillIndex": 10
