    "id": "SM-0f2ceda8d10c7a02",
    "section": "reading",
    "skill": "Paragraph function",
    "q": "What is the main function of paragraph 2?",
    "o": [
      "It qualifies the interpretation of the observation by introducing another possible influence.",
      "It replaces the observation with a contrary measurement.",
      "It supplies a manual for installing the procedure.",
      "It proves that all earlier records are inaccurate."
    ],
    "e": "Paragraf 2 membatasi penafsiran sebab dengan faktor alternatif.",
    "origin": "original",
    "passage": {
      "id": "SM-DR-R-14",
      "title": "Trail repairs",
      "text": "A team at a park management team had been concerned about walkers avoiding a damaged trail. The team repaired drainage at the wettest section. During a 8-week trial, use of the trail increased. Staff kept daily logs describing both the operation of the change and the conditions under which it was used. These records were intended to make the experience available for later examination, rather than leave the discussion dependent on the recollection of one unusually successful day.\n\nThe observation did not settle every question about the change. The result could also have been affected by an unusually dry observation period. A comparison between the period before the change and the period after it would therefore combine two differences: the new procedure and the surrounding conditions. Counting more observations of the same combination would make that combination better described, but would not by itself separate the contributions of its components. The team kept the outcome in the report while distinguishing the observation from a claim about its cause. The figures were preliminary: they came from the first round and would be reviewed after further observations.\n\nThe proposed next investigation was to inspect trail use and condition after comparable rainfall. The staff would define the outcome in the same way across the comparison and retain records of relevant conditions. A useful question was whether the observed difference would remain when those conditions were made comparable. This question was narrower than deciding whether the procedure was best for every institution, every user, or every future period. The proposed comparison would supply evidence about the specified setting; applying it elsewhere would require considering how that other setting differed."
    },
    "solution": {
      "steps": [
        "Paragraf 2 membatasi penafsiran sebab dengan faktor alternatif."
      ],
      "evidence": "The result could also have been affected by an unusually dry observation period."
    },
    "difficulty": "foundation",
    "drillOnly": true,
    "edition": "drills-2026-10",
    "drillIndex": 14
