    "id": "SM-a1fd664365308d9a",
    "section": "reading",
    "skill": "Main idea",
    "q": "Which statement best captures the purpose of the passage?",
    "o": [
      "To evaluate the trial addressing inconsistent times for reading gauges and identify a more informative comparison.",
      "To provide detailed instructions for implementing the change at a volunteer weather network.",
      "To establish that new gauges replacing damaged equipment fully explains the reported observation.",
      "To compare the financial costs of several institutions facing inconsistent times for reading gauges."
    ],
    "e": "Gagasan utama mencakup masalah, hasil percobaan, dan pengujian lanjutan. Petunjuk teknis, kepastian penyebab alternatif, dan perbandingan biaya bukan fokus bacaan.",
    "origin": "original",
    "passage": {
      "id": "SM-DR-R-33",
      "title": "Rain gauges",
      "text": "A team at a volunteer weather network had been concerned about inconsistent times for reading gauges. The team agreed on one daily reading time. During a 7-week trial, daily records became easier to compare. Staff kept daily logs describing both the operation of the change and the conditions under which it was used. These records were intended to make the experience available for later examination, rather than leave the discussion dependent on the recollection of one unusually successful day.\n\nThe observation did not settle every question about the change. The result could also have been affected by new gauges replacing damaged equipment. A comparison between the period before the change and the period after it would therefore combine two differences: the new procedure and the surrounding conditions. Counting more observations of the same combination would make that combination better described, but would not by itself separate the contributions of its components. The team kept the outcome in the report while distinguishing the observation from a claim about its cause. The proportion of successful cases was calculated from both the number of successes and the number of opportunities for success.\n\nThe proposed next investigation was to separate reading-time changes from equipment replacement. The staff would define the outcome in the same way across the comparison and retain records of relevant conditions. A useful question was whether the observed difference would remain when those conditions were made comparable. This question was narrower than deciding whether the procedure was best for every institution, every user, or every future period. The proposed comparison would supply evidence about the specified setting; applying it elsewhere would require considering how that other setting differed.\n\nThe report also distinguished practical usefulness from certainty about a mechanism. A team may have reasons to continue a trial while still testing the explanation for its results. Equally, identifying an alternative explanation does not establish that the alternative caused the whole result. The point of recording it is to specify what a more informative comparison would need to address. Neither the original observation nor the proposed test was presented as a guarantee of permanent success."
    },
    "solution": {
      "steps": [
        "Gagasan utama mencakup masalah, hasil percobaan, dan pengujian lanjutan. Petunjuk teknis, kepastian penyebab alternatif, dan perbandingan biaya bukan fokus bacaan."
      ],
      "evidence": "The proposed next investigation was to separate reading-time changes from equipment replacement."
    },
    "difficulty": "standard",
    "drillOnly": true,
    "edition": "drills-2026-10",
    "drillIndex": 33
