    "id": "SM-40dc587acf76fdb5",
    "section": "reading",
    "skill": "Main idea",
    "q": "Which statement best captures the purpose of the passage?",
    "o": [
      "To evaluate the trial addressing decisions being confused with proposals and identify a more informative comparison.",
      "To provide detailed instructions for implementing the change at a neighbourhood council.",
      "To establish that later meetings containing fewer disputed proposals fully explains the reported observation.",
      "To compare the financial costs of several institutions facing decisions being confused with proposals."
    ],
    "e": "Gagasan utama mencakup masalah, hasil percobaan, dan pengujian lanjutan. Petunjuk teknis, kepastian penyebab alternatif, dan perbandingan biaya bukan fokus bacaan.",
    "origin": "original",
    "passage": {
      "id": "SM-DR-R-43",
      "title": "Meeting summaries",
      "text": "A team at a neighbourhood council had been concerned about decisions being confused with proposals. The team separated decisions from proposals in minutes. During a 7-week trial, readers classified more statements correctly. Staff kept daily logs describing both the operation of the change and the conditions under which it was used. These records were intended to make the experience available for later examination, rather than leave the discussion dependent on the recollection of one unusually successful day.\n\nThe observation did not settle every question about the change. The result could also have been affected by later meetings containing fewer disputed proposals. A comparison between the period before the change and the period after it would therefore combine two differences: the new procedure and the surrounding conditions. Counting more observations of the same combination would make that combination better described, but would not by itself separate the contributions of its components. The team kept the outcome in the report while distinguishing the observation from a claim about its cause. The summary was selective: it included completed cases but omitted unfinished ones, a choice that readers needed to know.\n\nThe proposed next investigation was to test both formats on the same meeting content. The staff would define the outcome in the same way across the comparison and retain records of relevant conditions. A useful question was whether the observed difference would remain when those conditions were made comparable. This question was narrower than deciding whether the procedure was best for every institution, every user, or every future period. The proposed comparison would supply evidence about the specified setting; applying it elsewhere would require considering how that other setting differed.\n\nThe report also distinguished practical usefulness from certainty about a mechanism. A team may have reasons to continue a trial while still testing the explanation for its results. Equally, identifying an alternative explanation does not establish that the alternative caused the whole result. The point of recording it is to specify what a more informative comparison would need to address. Neither the original observation nor the proposed test was presented as a guarantee of permanent success.\n\nOne further distinction concerned the unit of analysis. A change in a combined total need not describe the experience of each subgroup, and an improvement in an average need not reveal the spread of individual outcomes. The authors therefore asked that any later summary state whose experience it represented and which activities its measurement included. This qualification was meant to make comparisons interpretable, rather than to dismiss the collection of numerical evidence."
    },
    "solution": {
      "steps": [
        "Gagasan utama mencakup masalah, hasil percobaan, dan pengujian lanjutan. Petunjuk teknis, kepastian penyebab alternatif, dan perbandingan biaya bukan fokus bacaan."
      ],
      "evidence": "The proposed next investigation was to test both formats on the same meeting content."
    },
    "difficulty": "challenge",
    "drillOnly": true,
    "edition": "drills-2026-10",
    "drillIndex": 43
