    "e": "Gagasan utama mencakup masalah, hasil percobaan, dan pengujian lanjutan. Petunjuk teknis, kepastian penyebab alternatif, dan perbandingan biaya bukan fokus bacaan.",
    "origin": "original",
    "passage": {
      "id": "SM-DR-R-45",
      "title": "Loan instructions",
      "text": "A team at a musical-instrument library had been concerned about borrowers missing instructions about fragile parts. The team placed handling notes beside the relevant parts. During a 4-week trial, fewer handling errors were recorded. Staff kept daily logs describing both the operation of the change and the conditions under which it was used. These records were intended to make the experience available for later examination, rather than leave the discussion dependent on the recollection of one unusually successful day.\n\nThe observation did not settle every question about the change. The result could also have been affected by later loans involving more experienced musicians. A comparison between the period before the change and the period after it would therefore combine two differences: the new procedure and the surrounding conditions. Counting more observations of the same combination would make that combination better described, but would not by itself separate the contributions of its components. The team kept the outcome in the report while distinguishing the observation from a claim about its cause. Recording the relevant conditions could mitigate the risk of misleading comparisons, although it would not eliminate every source of error.\n\nThe proposed next investigation was to compare users with similar instrument experience. The staff would define the outcome in the same way across the comparison and retain records of relevant conditions. A useful question was whether the observed difference would remain when those conditions were made comparable. This question was narrower than deciding whether the procedure was best for every institution, every user, or every future period. The proposed comparison would supply evidence about the specified setting; applying it elsewhere would require considering how that other setting differed.\n\nThe report also distinguished practical usefulness from certainty about a mechanism. A team may have reasons to continue a trial while still testing the explanation for its results. Equally, identifying an alternative explanation does not establish that the alternative caused the whole result. The point of recording it is to specify what a more informative comparison would need to address. Neither the original observation nor the proposed test was presented as a guarantee of permanent success.\n\nOne further distinction concerned the unit of analysis. A change in a combined total need not describe the experience of each subgroup, and an improvement in an average need not reveal the spread of individual outcomes. The authors therefore asked that any later summary state whose experience it represented and which activities its measurement included. This qualification was meant to make comparisons interpretable, rather than to dismiss the collection of numerical evidence."
    },
